<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Required because this fork is ad-hoc signed rather than Developer ID-signed. The hardened
	  runtime enables library validation, which only lets a process load libraries sharing its
	  Team ID; an ad-hoc signature has none, so dyld refuses to load the app's own bundled
	  Sparkle.framework and the process dies before main().

	  docs/RELEASING.md explains it in full, including why codesign's own verification does not
	  catch it.

	  Keep every comment in this file free of doubled hyphens. XML forbids them inside a
	  comment, and while Xcode's parser tolerates it, the one AMFI uses when codesign applies
	  entitlements does not: it fails with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error", naming a line
	  number in the comment rather than the real problem. That makes manual re-signing (see
	  scripts/install-local.sh) fail for a reason nothing about the message suggests.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
